1c7a4836 (2482 1793634168671 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f16c") (src . "read --ast: spans on every node, verbatim raw-md, one ref supplier\n\nEvery block node and every reference in the parsed tree carries one\n(span <start> <end>): half-open byte offsets into the UTF-8 encoding of\nthe block's src, placed after the node's scalar elements and before its\nchildren. A block's span runs from the start of its first line to the\nend of its last line's terminator, container prefixes and interior\nlines included; a reference's from the first byte of [[ to the byte\nafter ]], counted on src as written, before escapes and entities are\ndecoded. Strings, em, strong, code, link and br carry none. The origin\nmap behind this gives every line a taker walks its place in the top\nsrc, so a quote in a list in a quote maps to the top src and never to\nthe joined child string it was handed.\n\nraw-md is verbatim: its text is exactly the bytes of its span, CRLF and\nevery container prefix kept, and it carries a (refs ...) clause, the\nreferences in it found and resolved as in a paragraph; an indented code\nblock's is empty. Nothing inside code and nothing after a backslash is\na reference. The printer writes raw-md text as it is, and its line-start\nescape fires only when the line's first character is text-written, so a\ncode span, a ref lexeme or a tab-led continuation line prints back\nunchanged. Printed back with the spans left out, a parsed tree parses to\nthe same tree, with the two known exceptions the README names.\n\nmd-refs and line-refs are gone; md-ref-nodes, the references the parser\nfound in document order, is the one supplier; the ref relation and\nmd-referrers read it instead of lexing a second time. ast-with-targets\nplaces a reference's target before its span and visits a raw-md's refs\nclause.\n\nTests: test/ast-spans.sc is new (72 rows: byte endpoints as literals on\nhand-written sources and on the corpus, the a1 round trip, the memory\nstore's 3087 sources against the 57 known emphasis-delimiter sources,\nthe cost line); md1, read-ast, a1-import and the a1 dump follow the new\nshape; rows-baseline gains the ast-spans row.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 607))))
